        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Ironweed (film)\n- Places: Albany, New York; Jay Street at Lark Street; Albany Rural Cemetery; North Broadway; 893 Broadway\n- Buildings: Miss Albany Diner; Lil's Diner\n\nFacts:\n- Miss Albany Diner, formerly known as Lil's Diner, is a historic diner in Albany, New York.\n- Miss Albany Diner was built in 1941 and is located at 893 Broadway, one of the oldest streets in Albany.\n- Major portions of Ironweed were shot on location in Albany, New York.\n- Ironweed included filming at Jay Street at Lark Street, Albany Rural Cemetery, and the Miss Albany Diner on North Broadway.",
